/ActualText (A personal information inventory is a structured record or database that organizations maintain to catalog and manage all the personal data they collect, process, store, or share. It serves as a comprehensive list detailing the types of personal information held, the purposes for which it is used, the legal basis for processing, retention periods, and any third parties with whom the data is shared. This inventory helps organizations ensure compliance with data protection regulations, assess data risks, and implement appropriate data protection measures.)
