<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Organizations must conduct a comprehensive analysis to identify and document all relevant data protection legal requirements applicable to their operations. This involves researching and understanding data protection laws in jurisdictions where they operate or process personal data, mapping out data flows to pinpoint where legal obligations apply throughout the data lifecycle, and documenting specific requirements such as lawful bases for processing, individuals' rights, data security measures, breach notification obligations, and rules for international data transfers. Implementation of compliance measures, including policies, procedures, and staff training, ensures adherence to these requirements. Regular monitoring and updating of documentation and practices are essential to adapt to evolving regulatory landscapes and maintain robust data protection practices that safeguard individuals' privacy rights.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
