/ActualText (A privacy risk assessment report is a structured evaluation that systematically analyzes how an organization handles personal data across its operations and with third-party services. It identifies potential vulnerabilities, threats, and risks to individuals' privacy, assesses the likelihood and impact of these risks, and recommends mitigating measures. The report serves to provide an overview of the organization's privacy risk posture, support compliance with data protection regulations, guide the implementation of effective data protection measures, and enhance transparency and accountability in data processing practices.)
